{"entryId":"2919","paragraphs":[{"sourceId":"heilprin:sefaria-warsaw:ta:2919:1","sourceSha256":"7c28f6a990415d2dc009037890585ba189aafbdb0e4916b3f45b6359302f67fd","englishSha256":"7a85c69eeaab8fe2cd714ac2f054e7b74c0d2a01700b658dc1e73ba8c7d5b291","citations":[{"id":"2919:1:link-001","he":[29,39],"en":[45,61],"target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Bava_Metzia_114a.4"},"reference":"Bava Metzia 114a:4","assessment":"The base text names Yaakov bar Pada. The source entry compares the alternative name Akiva.","evidence":[{"reference":"Bava Metzia 114a:4","target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Bava_Metzia_114a.4"},"witness":"William Davidson Edition - Vocalized Aramaic"}]},{"id":"2919:1:link-002","he":[59,68],"en":[110,118],"target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Berakhot_55b.16"},"reference":"Berakhot 55b:16","assessment":"The cited chain directly includes Akiva and Panda. Heilprin records a different chain under Bizna.","evidence":[{"reference":"Berakhot 55b:16","target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Berakhot_55b.16"},"witness":"William Davidson Edition - Vocalized Aramaic"},{"reference":"Seder HaDorot 700:1","target":{"entry":700,"paragraph":1},"witness":"Pinned Warsaw digital witness"}]}],"inlineHebrew":[0,1],"holds":[],"notes":[{"text":"Bava Metzia 114a:4 gives Yaakov reporting in the name of bar Pada, just as Heilprin explicitly cautions. It does not support linking this report to Akiva as a person.","references":[],"urls":[]},{"text":"Berakhot 55b:16 gives the three reported names in precisely this order, and then a longer chain. The local Bizna article records a Yuḥasin alternate Ukva/Parna chain. Do not collapse the two reports in this entry.","references":[],"urls":[]},{"text":"The base text names Yaakov bar Pada. The source entry compares the alternative name Akiva.","references":[],"urls":[]},{"text":"The cited chain directly includes Akiva and Panda. Heilprin records a different chain under Bizna.","references":[],"urls":[]}],"comparisonEvidence":[{"refer